  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains two versions of this program: the GuidedPath version (180 quarter credits) and the FlexPath option (90 program points). This ledger covers the GuidedPath quarter-credit version. FlexPath program points are not one of the supported credit systems and were not converted.",
    "The capture lists MAT1050 and MAT2051 as required courses under General Education Requirements but does not explicitly say they count toward the 45 general education quarter credits. The remaining general education block of 33 credits is inferred from the totals: 45 + 54 + 30 + 39 + 12 = 180.",
    "General education requires a minimum of 4 quarter credits from each of the four categories (Communication, Humanities, Natural Science and Mathematics, Social Science). The capture does not say how the required MAT courses satisfy the Natural Science and Mathematics minimum.",
    "Total requires a minimum of 54 quarter credits from the 3000-level and above. Which elective and general education choices satisfy this is not specified.",
    "No residency or institutional-credit requirement (courses that must be completed at Capella) is stated in the capture.",
    "Specific courses that qualify for the 30-credit specialization block are not listed; only the subject areas are given.",
    "The optional Honors Pathway (at least 15 quarter credits: PHI-H2005, COM-H4005, SOC-H3005) applies toward general education and was not included as a standard requirement.",
    "Course prerequisites are referenced but not detailed in the capture.",
    "The capstone courses must be taken during the student's final two quarters (a sequencing rule, not a residency rule)."
  ],
